WEBVTT

00:29.238 --> 00:30.572
LA's an immigrant city.

00:31.532 --> 00:33.616
From the Chumash to the Persians

00:33.617 --> 00:35.869
to the Vietnamese
to everyone else in between.

00:36.620 --> 00:37.746
This is where they come.

00:40.916 --> 00:44.669
A writer once said, "Los Angeles
gives the feeling of the future

00:44.670 --> 00:46.463
more strongly than any city I know of.

00:47.005 --> 00:48.464
A bad future, too."

00:48.465 --> 00:50.008
Wait for me, right?

00:50.884 --> 00:53.052
- Thought I told you--
- Fuck y'all!

00:53.053 --> 00:55.304
- But, I don't know about that.
- Hey.

00:55.305 --> 00:57.015
I'm an immigrant too, I guess.

00:57.599 --> 00:59.434
I think LA's got a lot of good to it.

01:01.687 --> 01:03.020
There he is.

01:03.021 --> 01:04.022
Let's do this.

01:07.943 --> 01:12.406
I'll admit it though.
It's a hard town, no argument there.

02:29.399 --> 02:34.696
And now the purple dusk
Of twilight time

02:35.489 --> 02:40.452
Steals across the meadows of my heart

02:42.246 --> 02:47.918
High up in the sky
The little stars climb

02:48.502 --> 02:53.465
Always reminding me that we're apart

02:56.802 --> 03:01.640
You wander down the lane
And far away

03:02.391 --> 03:03.392
Sweet pool.

03:07.813 --> 03:10.481
Hey. So what did your car guy say?

03:10.482 --> 03:12.860
Listen, most times,
a whip like that rolls in...

03:13.694 --> 03:17.155
the mechanic makes a sad face, takes
whatever it really costs and adds a zero.

03:18.365 --> 03:20.408
But, Sugar, today you are in luck,

03:20.409 --> 03:21.493
'cause my guy Billy...

03:22.536 --> 03:24.203
I mean, he's like an honest Gandalf.

03:24.204 --> 03:25.746
I thought you were going
for an oil change.

03:25.747 --> 03:29.250
You can't leave a car like that
up on blocks for six months

03:29.251 --> 03:31.669
and expect her to be up and running
with just an oil change.

03:31.670 --> 03:33.380
All right? But she's good now.
She's perfect.

03:36.758 --> 03:38.010
All right.

03:42.389 --> 03:43.390
There she goes.

03:48.562 --> 03:50.146
So you stay here, huh?

03:50.147 --> 03:51.440
Live here.

03:52.524 --> 03:53.650
You live here?

03:55.652 --> 03:56.737
You must charge a lot.

03:57.613 --> 03:59.323
Industry rates, from what I'm told.

04:00.699 --> 04:01.992
Nice industry.

04:02.910 --> 04:03.911
It ain't bad.

04:11.168 --> 04:13.212
Hey. You want a job, Val?

04:14.338 --> 04:17.340
I gotta be somewhere in a couple hours,
but sure. What do you got?

04:17.341 --> 04:18.884
No, no, no. A job. Like a job-job.

04:20.511 --> 04:21.678
Working with me.

04:22.221 --> 04:24.556
You know? Ongoing position.

04:27.100 --> 04:30.604
No, I'm serious. I mean, we just met, but
you're disciplined, you're resourceful.

04:31.146 --> 04:33.148
And to be honest with you, I could...

04:33.899 --> 04:35.275
I could do with the help.

04:38.737 --> 04:39.738
Right.

04:40.781 --> 04:43.032
No, but I don't wanna presume.

04:43.033 --> 04:44.034
Not if you...

04:45.869 --> 04:46.953
No, I mean I'm...

04:46.954 --> 04:50.499
I'm always on the lookout for
new shit, new job opportunities.

04:51.416 --> 04:53.085
- So you'll think about it?
- For sure.

04:53.877 --> 04:55.545
Yeah, cool. Let me think on it.

04:55.546 --> 04:56.755
Good. Think about it.

04:57.381 --> 05:00.133
- Good.
- Good.

05:00.968 --> 05:01.969
Okay.

05:19.361 --> 05:21.905
Danny! Throw your hands up,
Danny. Come on.

05:23.657 --> 05:24.658
Move your feet.

05:26.994 --> 05:28.245
That's it. Move.

05:31.123 --> 05:32.457
Here we go.

05:33.750 --> 05:34.960
That's it. Come on.

05:37.462 --> 05:39.131
Move your feet. Move your feet.

05:46.972 --> 05:48.765
They call it the Sweet Science.

05:49.349 --> 05:51.727
It's brutal, but they call it sport.

05:52.436 --> 05:53.478
Danny.

05:55.272 --> 05:56.273
Danny!

05:56.815 --> 05:58.441
I gotta admit,

05:58.442 --> 06:01.360
whatever you wanna call it,
it's hard to look away.

06:01.361 --> 06:03.280
He's stealing drugs
from the fucking hospital?

06:04.031 --> 06:05.490
It's the last place he was seen.

06:06.366 --> 06:09.202
Jesus. He's not always like this.

06:09.203 --> 06:11.746
- I mean, these days he is, but...
- You don't need to explain.

06:11.747 --> 06:14.416
I'm not explaining anything,
I'm just telling it like it is.

06:15.501 --> 06:16.502
Of course.

06:18.879 --> 06:21.798
And the police aren't looking for him?

06:22.508 --> 06:23.675
As far as I know.

06:25.260 --> 06:26.344
- Excuse me.
- Remember,

06:26.345 --> 06:28.179
when you're in there,
keep your feet moving.

06:28.180 --> 06:29.515
Hey, Tom. What do you got?

06:30.474 --> 06:32.808
Hands up, guts up. Keep your hands up.

06:32.809 --> 06:34.101
What's up, Coach?

06:34.102 --> 06:35.562
- Agent?
- I wish.

06:36.271 --> 06:38.314
No, just some guy helping with Ji.

06:38.315 --> 06:41.609
- Ji. Your crazy brother Ji, huh?
- Yeah.

06:41.610 --> 06:43.486
Listen, good job the other night.

06:43.487 --> 06:47.573
Eddie Mbanefo is two classes above you.

06:47.574 --> 06:50.619
Now, he moves like a cement pig,
but he's no tomato can.

06:51.787 --> 06:53.162
Thanks, Teddy.

06:53.163 --> 06:54.247
That guy was slow.

06:54.248 --> 06:56.040
Just had to work
his middle and stop his feet

06:56.041 --> 06:57.876
and then, pop, pop, come up high.

06:58.544 --> 07:00.461
Big things are coming for you, Danny.

07:00.462 --> 07:02.255
- Stay focused.
- Okay.

07:02.256 --> 07:04.132
- All right, I'll text when I'm there.
- All right.

07:04.842 --> 07:06.218
Okay, bye.

07:07.386 --> 07:08.803
- Sorry.
- So we're good, right?

07:08.804 --> 07:11.889
You'll just... you know, keep me updated?

07:11.890 --> 07:15.852
Definitely, yeah. I gotta go.
Thank you for letting me come by.

07:15.853 --> 07:16.936
Sure.

07:16.937 --> 07:19.606
Yo, that call. Was it about Ji?

07:21.400 --> 07:23.109
I'll let you know.

07:23.110 --> 07:24.111
Okay.

07:32.578 --> 07:34.204
Everything comes to an end.

07:36.290 --> 07:38.083
Sooner than you think sometimes.

07:41.128 --> 07:44.882
From the side suns of Andromeda,
to the detamorphs on Paloma.

07:47.801 --> 07:48.886
Everything dies.

07:53.098 --> 07:54.099
But still...

07:57.144 --> 07:59.229
I'm hoping I don't find Ji here.

08:05.235 --> 08:06.737
They're bringing him.

08:10.616 --> 08:12.533
- Tom Flybjerg.
- Fucking...

08:12.534 --> 08:15.620
I helped him a few years ago
when his wife went missing hiking in Ojai.

08:15.621 --> 08:17.705
Say, you know how
to put stuff on Instagram?

08:17.706 --> 08:20.000
Turned out,
she'd only gone missing from Tom.

08:21.919 --> 08:23.669
Hey, Flybjerg, coming in.

08:23.670 --> 08:24.671
Here we go.

08:28.675 --> 08:30.511
Early 20s Asian male.

08:36.642 --> 08:37.643
Good resemblance.

08:39.061 --> 08:40.894
All right. Good news.

08:40.895 --> 08:41.938
Not for him.

08:43.106 --> 08:45.608
You said it was a gang hit?
He doesn't look like a banger.

08:45.609 --> 08:48.695
He's probably a civilian.
Wrong place, wrong time kind of thing.

08:49.655 --> 08:51.364
- That his stuff?
- Yeah.

08:51.365 --> 08:54.909
Wallet, photos, a few bills, a phone card.
But no photo ID.

08:54.910 --> 08:55.911
- Can I?
- Yeah.

09:03.335 --> 09:07.172
He's an immigrant. Recent.
He's probably still waiting on his papers.

09:07.840 --> 09:10.716
Trace the activity on this phone card
and you can find his parents.

09:10.717 --> 09:12.970
It'll just be one number
he called over and over.

09:13.595 --> 09:14.679
Fair.

09:14.680 --> 09:15.972
On a brighter note,

09:15.973 --> 09:18.808
in the "arc of history bends
towards justice" category,

09:18.809 --> 09:20.017
Katie, where's the shooter?

09:20.018 --> 09:21.019
Over here.

09:22.312 --> 09:24.231
It's like fucking Mardi Gras in here.

09:25.357 --> 09:27.901
LAPD ran up on him two blocks away.

09:35.659 --> 09:36.784
"Ez4"?

09:36.785 --> 09:39.204
Gang tat probably. I'll ask around.

09:42.249 --> 09:44.293
A gang member killing a civilian?

09:45.002 --> 09:46.003
It happens.

09:47.171 --> 09:49.464
Initiation, get your wings sort of thing.

09:50.299 --> 09:53.260
Or he's just an idiot, shot the wrong guy.

09:59.224 --> 10:00.600
You mind?

10:00.601 --> 10:01.602
Go ahead.

10:10.527 --> 10:14.990
Sometimes it still works
if he's just... dead.

10:17.409 --> 10:18.911
Don't ask how we learned that.

10:24.583 --> 10:26.209
I think you were right.

10:26.210 --> 10:27.460
About what?

10:27.461 --> 10:28.670
They shot the wrong guy.

10:30.005 --> 10:33.341
I guess I was still hoping whatever
trouble Ji had gotten himself into

10:33.342 --> 10:35.093
was of the self-inflicted variety.

10:36.011 --> 10:38.137
But someone really is after him.

10:38.138 --> 10:39.181
Someone serious.

10:42.768 --> 10:43.936
He's right to be afraid.

10:45.395 --> 10:48.649
Still, it gave me a thought
on where to look next.

10:49.816 --> 10:50.984
Or where to look again.

10:56.740 --> 10:57.741
Damn it!

11:00.661 --> 11:01.662
Hey.

11:02.162 --> 11:03.371
You okay?

11:03.372 --> 11:06.959
I'm fine. I just got fired,
so, kinda having a bad day.

11:07.876 --> 11:09.586
I'm sorry. That's too bad.

11:10.337 --> 11:11.588
- I got you.
- Thanks.

11:12.589 --> 11:13.674
Thank you.

11:15.676 --> 11:17.177
- Thank you. Yeah.
- Yeah. All right.

11:19.263 --> 11:20.680
Hey. Good luck.

11:20.681 --> 11:21.682
Thanks.

11:29.857 --> 11:31.107
Blaine.

11:31.108 --> 11:35.237
"If it's December 1941 in Casablanca,
what time is it in New York?"

11:37.322 --> 11:38.323
"My watch stopped."

11:39.408 --> 11:40.491
- You saw the film?
- Yes!

11:40.492 --> 11:42.243
- What'd you think?
- Phenomenal.

11:42.244 --> 11:43.245
Good.

11:44.037 --> 11:45.747
I have a favor to ask.

11:52.754 --> 11:53.755
That's him.

11:54.840 --> 11:56.090
Uh-huh.

11:56.091 --> 11:57.466
- That's your guy?
- Yeah.

11:57.467 --> 11:59.010
Leaving the fourth floor.

11:59.011 --> 12:00.553
You have cameras in the stairwell?

12:00.554 --> 12:01.637
No.

12:01.638 --> 12:04.098
All right, can you show me
the exit the stairs lead to?

12:04.099 --> 12:05.100
Okay.

12:16.069 --> 12:17.237
Where'd he go?

12:17.988 --> 12:22.326
I mean it's been nine, ten minutes,
and he's still...

12:23.911 --> 12:24.912
There he is.

12:28.373 --> 12:30.459
Why'd it take him so long
to get down the stairs?

12:31.001 --> 12:32.753
He must've gone to another floor.

12:34.880 --> 12:36.590
- Check the cameras?
- Yeah.

12:38.175 --> 12:39.510
You're right. Here he is.

12:41.428 --> 12:43.722
Exiting the fifth-floor stairwell.

12:47.893 --> 12:49.685
Here he is a few minutes later.

12:49.686 --> 12:50.896
Stop. Go back.

12:52.397 --> 12:54.900
Okay, go forward, slowly.
Slow, slow, slow, stop.

13:00.447 --> 13:01.781
Something spooked him.

13:01.782 --> 13:02.783
Yeah.

13:05.869 --> 13:09.872
He doesn't show up
at the elevator or the nurse's station,

13:09.873 --> 13:15.629
so wherever he went for those few minutes
have to be off that hallway.

13:16.255 --> 13:17.548
A hallway on the fifth floor.

13:40.195 --> 13:43.657
"Jesus Alejandro Jaquez, 22 years old.

13:44.741 --> 13:46.576
Admitted April 27th."

13:46.577 --> 13:48.161
Three days before Ji was here.

13:49.079 --> 13:51.247
"Patient arrived
with multiple gunshot wounds.

13:51.248 --> 13:54.834
Multiple transfusions.
Intubation due to perforated lung.

13:54.835 --> 13:56.545
Emergency splenectomy."

14:05.679 --> 14:06.680
Poor kid.

14:07.514 --> 14:08.515
He didn't make it.

14:13.812 --> 14:15.314
What were you doing, Ji?

14:42.758 --> 14:44.718
How does a dead man take a picture?

14:48.680 --> 14:49.681
Unless...

14:51.225 --> 14:52.434
someone else was there.

14:54.895 --> 14:56.896
All right. Now we're looking
for someone else.

14:56.897 --> 14:59.106
Visitor, fifth floor, same time as my guy.

14:59.107 --> 15:03.111
It was late, so nurses, orderlies...

15:14.915 --> 15:16.166
Him.

15:24.049 --> 15:26.176
He's hiding his face from the cameras.

15:28.804 --> 15:29.888
Who is he?

15:45.028 --> 15:46.029
Who is that?

16:19.938 --> 16:21.647
Ji-Ho! There he is!

16:21.648 --> 16:22.857
Hey, guys.

16:22.858 --> 16:24.400
Rocky too!

16:24.401 --> 16:25.484
Hey, Lucy.

16:25.485 --> 16:26.694
Hi, Danny.

16:26.695 --> 16:29.030
Hungry?
I have some Sundubu Jjigae left over.

16:29.031 --> 16:30.406
I'm all right, thank you.

16:30.407 --> 16:32.325
Just wanted to say good night.

16:32.326 --> 16:33.327
Goodnight.

16:33.994 --> 16:34.995
By the way.

16:35.996 --> 16:37.289
And so rent?

16:38.332 --> 16:39.333
Is coming soon?

16:40.125 --> 16:41.919
You haven't received our rent, yet?

16:42.961 --> 16:45.296
Ji-Seok didn't pay you?

16:45.297 --> 16:47.298
Are you fucking serious, Ji?

16:47.299 --> 16:50.093
Where the hell are you?
Call me back right fucking now!

16:51.303 --> 16:52.679
Son of a bitch! Fuck!

16:56.016 --> 16:58.810
It's not easy being on your own sometimes.

16:59.978 --> 17:01.896
Before, there were thousands of us.

17:01.897 --> 17:06.358
I could always come home
and find someone to talk to. Now?

17:06.359 --> 17:07.902
You have no new messages.

17:07.903 --> 17:09.946
Well, now I have work to do.

17:11.740 --> 17:13.951
Who are these people after Ji?

17:16.286 --> 17:18.703
LA's got street gangs.
Everyone knows that.

17:18.704 --> 17:20.998
From 18th street to Glendale.

17:20.999 --> 17:22.751
From Long Beach up into Ventura.

17:24.044 --> 17:27.881
Drugs and guns and senseless drive-bys
is what we're told on the news.

17:29.091 --> 17:30.676
But that's not the whole story.

17:31.718 --> 17:34.555
Right or wrong, gangs are like families.

17:35.222 --> 17:37.139
And families make you feel
part of something.

17:37.140 --> 17:39.393
And that's a powerful thing.

17:41.311 --> 17:44.606
Like I said, it's hard being on your own.

18:11.884 --> 18:13.093
Hello again.

18:16.138 --> 18:17.139
Hello.

18:20.642 --> 18:23.019
- Made up your mind?
- Just the usual, please, Eric.

18:23.020 --> 18:25.062
Mung beans with ghee and a side of papaya.

18:25.063 --> 18:26.190
And I wanted to ask.

18:27.608 --> 18:29.234
How did the callback go?

18:30.068 --> 18:31.277
I didn't get it.

18:31.278 --> 18:32.403
No!

18:32.404 --> 18:34.739
- Aw, I know you wanted that one.
- I know.

18:34.740 --> 18:36.240
I thought I had it too.

18:36.241 --> 18:38.910
That sucks. I remember Sydney Greenstreet,

18:38.911 --> 18:41.245
he didn't get his big break
until The Maltese Falcon,

18:41.246 --> 18:42.706
when he was what, 61?

18:43.665 --> 18:45.501
Never know what's gonna
happen next, you know?

18:50.005 --> 18:51.381
That was nice of you.

18:52.966 --> 18:54.051
What? What was?

18:55.552 --> 18:58.096
What you said.
I bet you turned his whole night around.

19:03.268 --> 19:05.521
Men don't usually like being called nice.

19:06.355 --> 19:08.857
Not all men. Not only men,

19:09.816 --> 19:11.860
but they think it's a sign of weakness.

19:12.528 --> 19:13.862
Only, I think it's the opposite.

19:14.446 --> 19:16.073
It's a powerful quality.

19:16.657 --> 19:18.367
This world could use a lot more of it.

19:20.452 --> 19:21.995
At least that's my experience.

19:25.374 --> 19:27.793
- How was everything tonight?
- Thank you. Delicious.

20:14.006 --> 20:15.465
You're nice too.

20:21.930 --> 20:22.931
You're not nice?

20:25.350 --> 20:28.270
I don't think it's the first thing
people would say about me.

20:33.108 --> 20:34.735
What would they say?

20:38.071 --> 20:41.866
Hardworking, passionate, humanitarian.

20:41.867 --> 20:42.950
Wow.

20:42.951 --> 20:44.661
Oh, my God. I sound so boring.

20:45.370 --> 20:46.621
No, you don't.

20:46.622 --> 20:48.123
Okay, let me try again.

20:49.416 --> 20:50.834
They would say...

20:51.710 --> 20:55.047
she enjoys talking
to nice men in restaurants.

21:02.846 --> 21:04.388
I'm sorry, I have to take this.

21:04.389 --> 21:05.390
Of course.

21:06.308 --> 21:07.684
To be continued.

21:12.773 --> 21:13.857
That was weird.

21:17.903 --> 21:19.153
No, no, no.

21:19.154 --> 21:20.781
That's not allowed.

21:28.705 --> 21:29.706
Fuck.

21:42.511 --> 21:44.847
Yo, yo, yo!
So what's up, champ? You in or what?

21:46.974 --> 21:48.724
Is there room for me on the next one?

21:48.725 --> 21:51.143
Yeah, baby! We actually
got a gig tomorrow night.

21:51.144 --> 21:53.980
You wanna make that cheddar?
I'll come pick you up.

21:53.981 --> 21:56.107
- All right, I'm down.
- Sick.

21:56.108 --> 21:57.526
I'll see you on the flip, bitch.

22:37.649 --> 22:39.484
Good morning, Senator Pavich.

22:46.700 --> 22:49.036
Former senator, I should say.

22:51.038 --> 22:53.874
He's now the CEO
of a brand new tech company.

22:55.250 --> 22:56.710
They put out a press release

22:57.211 --> 23:01.048
dedicated to developing brand new
solutions to age-old problems.

23:04.176 --> 23:07.012
So, he's either working on
a cure for cancer or...

23:09.097 --> 23:10.098
or what?

23:32.913 --> 23:34.039
Nice meeting you.

23:34.540 --> 23:36.041
Whatever it is,

23:36.625 --> 23:37.960
it looks like he's hiring.

23:42.798 --> 23:44.216
I should probably go.

23:45.092 --> 23:46.468
Clock's ticking on Ji Moon.

23:52.224 --> 23:55.059
You've reached Danny Moon.
Leave a message.

23:55.060 --> 23:56.269
Danny, it's Sugar.

23:56.270 --> 23:58.438
I've been trying to reach you.
Call me when you get this.

23:59.439 --> 24:02.860
Figured my best lead was to try and learn
something about Jesus Jaquez,

24:03.443 --> 24:05.779
the kid who died
in that hospital room with Ji.

24:06.655 --> 24:09.032
I got a next of kin address from Hannah.

25:01.835 --> 25:02.836
Mrs. Jaquez.

25:03.253 --> 25:04.337
Yes?

25:04.338 --> 25:06.255
My condolences about Jesus.

25:06.256 --> 25:07.466
My name is John.

25:08.258 --> 25:11.053
May I come in
and ask a few questions about him?

25:12.346 --> 25:13.555
Only take a moment?

25:16.225 --> 25:17.434
Come in.

25:27.069 --> 25:28.362
Poor woman.

25:28.862 --> 25:31.240
Grief. I'm familiar.

25:32.324 --> 25:35.702
When I first lost my sister,
I could barely move.

25:51.134 --> 25:52.135
Señora.

25:52.970 --> 25:56.056
Would it be possible to see Jesus' room?

25:57.015 --> 25:58.016
Thank you.

26:17.035 --> 26:18.412
Aztec art.

26:23.667 --> 26:24.877
He had interests.

26:29.464 --> 26:30.465
A home.

26:34.887 --> 26:36.013
He was loved.

26:52.863 --> 26:54.989
I'm sorry to bother you
any more than I have,

26:54.990 --> 26:58.785
but I'm hoping to spare someone else
from the pain you're suffering.

26:59.745 --> 27:00.746
I'm listening.

27:01.747 --> 27:02.748
Thank you.

27:07.377 --> 27:08.670
You recognize this person?

27:09.129 --> 27:11.465
Did you ever see him with Jesus?

27:16.803 --> 27:17.804
What about him?

27:30.484 --> 27:31.984
The picture

27:31.985 --> 27:33.110
in the bedroom.

27:33.111 --> 27:34.195
The woman?

27:34.196 --> 27:36.031
Sandra.

27:37.115 --> 27:38.116
His mom.

27:39.034 --> 27:40.117
Your daughter?

27:40.118 --> 27:41.370
Yes.

27:42.120 --> 27:43.204
Where is she?

27:43.205 --> 27:44.288
Streets.

27:44.289 --> 27:45.749
Drugs.

27:46.166 --> 27:47.209
Crazy.

27:50.212 --> 27:52.548
Was Jesus still in touch with her at all?

27:53.048 --> 27:54.882
Yes, they were best friends.

27:54.883 --> 27:56.218
Confidants.

27:58.011 --> 28:00.222
She called him "Chuy."

28:00.681 --> 28:01.682
"Chuy?"

28:18.115 --> 28:20.117
Can I do something for you?

28:21.743 --> 28:23.203
Like what?

29:29.186 --> 29:30.187
Hey.

29:34.107 --> 29:35.108
Hey.

29:37.319 --> 29:40.447
I'd like you to make a phone call
to your boss, like you did before.

29:41.907 --> 29:43.574
I ain't got no boss, G.

29:43.575 --> 29:45.701
I'm a CEO with a pension plan.

29:45.702 --> 29:47.496
Uh-huh. You seen this?

29:51.792 --> 29:52.959
You have.

29:52.960 --> 29:54.211
You take this photo?

29:59.216 --> 30:00.217
Nah, you didn't.

30:00.843 --> 30:03.719
All right. So what I'm asking
is that you tell your boss

30:03.720 --> 30:05.472
I wanna talk to the person who did.

30:07.182 --> 30:08.183
Here.

30:08.809 --> 30:10.227
Take it. I'm not the police.

30:10.894 --> 30:13.480
I heard there's been a misunderstanding.
I just want to clear it up.

30:15.232 --> 30:16.233
Okay.

30:17.401 --> 30:18.610
Let's clear it up then.

30:21.446 --> 30:24.616
Meantime, G? You probably wanna
get right the fuck out of here.

31:14.208 --> 31:15.791
Hey. I've been calling you.

31:15.792 --> 31:17.711
My bad, man. I've been busy.

31:18.921 --> 31:20.589
I got a lead I wanna ask you about.

31:21.173 --> 31:22.507
Sure, but I got work.

31:22.508 --> 31:24.383
A friend's about to pick me up
in a sec, so...

31:24.384 --> 31:25.761
Okay. I'll make it quick.

31:29.223 --> 31:33.684
You ever heard Ji mention the Ez4s?

31:33.685 --> 31:35.854
- The what?
- Ez4s, LA street gang.

31:36.480 --> 31:38.565
Yeah, your brother's on their radar
for some reason.

31:39.191 --> 31:41.693
A street gang? Are you fucking serious?

31:42.653 --> 31:45.488
I don't know what his involvement is yet.
He may not have done anything wrong--

31:45.489 --> 31:47.574
You told me he ripped drugs
off a hospital, right?

31:48.700 --> 31:50.076
- He did.
- What are you talking about

31:50.077 --> 31:53.163
he didn't do anything wrong? Ji's been
doing shit wrong for fucking years.

31:55.582 --> 31:56.583
Sorry.

32:00.754 --> 32:01.755
Fuck.

32:07.135 --> 32:08.136
You all right?

32:12.474 --> 32:14.309
Something else you want to tell me about?

32:17.312 --> 32:21.275
What are you, a fucking shrink now?
I haven't even paid you for the PI part.

32:22.401 --> 32:23.652
Don't worry about the money.

32:24.736 --> 32:26.988
Yeah, well, you're rich,
so you can say that.

32:26.989 --> 32:27.990
That's not why.

32:28.866 --> 32:29.867
No?

32:31.743 --> 32:34.287
How many of those expensive-ass suits
do you own?

32:34.288 --> 32:35.289
How many exactly?

32:36.707 --> 32:37.708
I don't know.

32:38.792 --> 32:40.210
'Cause you're rich, bro.

32:41.086 --> 32:43.380
Look, my friend's about to be here.
Thanks for checking in.

32:48.844 --> 32:50.554
Listen, Danny. Whatever's happening...

32:52.097 --> 32:53.974
Whatever it is that's going on, just...

32:55.559 --> 32:56.560
let me help you.

32:58.687 --> 32:59.688
No.

33:07.696 --> 33:09.156
Fucking Ji.

33:12.618 --> 33:15.036
Hey, there he is.

33:15.037 --> 33:16.330
Welcome back, champ.

33:34.932 --> 33:36.016
Okay, coming up.

33:45.734 --> 33:47.653
All right, bitches. Let's get to work.

33:54.034 --> 33:56.828
Yo, yo, yo, come on, chill!
Chill, bro! What the fuck?

33:57.996 --> 33:59.873
- Get the fuck back.
- What are y'all doing, man?

34:01.416 --> 34:03.669
Get the fuck off me, man! Fuck!

34:06.129 --> 34:07.130
Yo, chill!

34:11.051 --> 34:12.261
Let's go, let's go, let's go.

34:13.887 --> 34:15.013
Ay, yo, let's go.

34:15.681 --> 34:16.723
Let's go, come on.

34:17.224 --> 34:19.059
Get all that in the truck. Let's go.

34:30.112 --> 34:31.905
Yo, where did that guard come from?

34:32.406 --> 34:35.491
I didn't see him, and then he was...
He was right up on me.

34:35.492 --> 34:38.410
It's all right, man, chill.
You handled the fuck out of him.

34:38.411 --> 34:39.663
Fuck.

35:02.769 --> 35:03.770
Hey.

35:05.189 --> 35:06.190
Thank you.

35:15.490 --> 35:17.534
So, I stole some bathrobes from the pool.

35:19.411 --> 35:21.163
I just took a bunch of them.
Piled them up.

35:22.289 --> 35:24.833
Walked right through.
I mean, no one said shit.

35:25.417 --> 35:26.752
I'm gonna sell them on eBay.

35:29.213 --> 35:30.296
Cool.

35:30.297 --> 35:31.423
Okay.

35:34.009 --> 35:35.135
What's going on here?

35:38.222 --> 35:40.557
Sometimes I make mistakes,
but most of the time

35:41.725 --> 35:43.435
I see people real well.

35:47.523 --> 35:48.565
You see people.

35:53.779 --> 35:55.530
What do you see in me?

35:55.531 --> 35:56.823
More than a thief.

35:59.910 --> 36:02.036
Yeah. You got that right.

36:02.037 --> 36:03.247
And I need a partner.

36:04.706 --> 36:07.792
In private investigation.
I don't even know what's...

36:07.793 --> 36:09.127
I'll teach you.

36:09.628 --> 36:12.463
All right, you got a camera?
Not a phone camera. An actual camera.

36:12.464 --> 36:14.258
No. I know what you mean.
Yeah, I can find one.

36:15.217 --> 36:16.468
You got a car?

36:17.135 --> 36:18.428
A not-stolen one?

36:18.929 --> 36:20.346
Sure.

36:20.347 --> 36:21.348
All right.

36:27.980 --> 36:29.356
Does that figure look okay?

36:35.028 --> 36:36.613
- Yeah?
- Per week?

36:39.575 --> 36:42.619
Okay. You start tomorrow.

36:44.079 --> 36:45.414
I've done some things.

36:47.958 --> 36:50.043
More than bathrobes and cars.

36:50.794 --> 36:52.129
I've done some things too.

36:56.592 --> 36:57.593
All right.

36:58.635 --> 36:59.678
Let's fucking go.

37:00.554 --> 37:01.680
- Okay.
- All right.

37:06.018 --> 37:07.394
Caesar salad and New York strip.

37:08.228 --> 37:09.646
I put it on your room.

37:44.348 --> 37:46.683
You have no new messages.

38:00.864 --> 38:01.948
Sugar.

38:01.949 --> 38:04.743
I heard you want to talk
to the man who took that photo.

38:05.869 --> 38:06.870
Yeah.

38:07.538 --> 38:09.039
Grab a pen. Here's an address.

38:12.626 --> 38:13.627
Go ahead.

38:18.090 --> 38:20.384
I have a bad feeling about this case.

38:20.926 --> 38:23.470
Says the hero in every PI movie ever made.

38:27.599 --> 38:29.226
And he's usually right to worry.

38:30.936 --> 38:34.147
It only goes from bad to worse
from that point on.

38:35.816 --> 38:36.817
But he keeps going.

38:37.860 --> 38:38.861
He doesn't stop.

38:39.611 --> 38:41.154
Not on a case like this.

38:43.365 --> 38:44.366
He can't.

38:45.325 --> 38:47.452
He's a PI. And the PI has to know.

38:51.540 --> 38:52.791
And so he'll keep going...

38:55.502 --> 38:56.879
and going...

39:04.845 --> 39:06.471
right up until the very end.

40:20.504 --> 40:22.422
And now the purple dusk
Of twilight time

40:26.552 --> 40:30.722
Steals across the meadows of my heart

40:33.392 --> 40:38.480
High up in the sky
The little stars climb

40:39.523 --> 40:46.113
Always reminding me that we're apart ♪

40:47.823 --> 40:52.286
You wandered down the lane
And far away

40:54.663 --> 40:59.751
Leaving me a song that will not die

41:03.046 --> 41:09.052
Love is now the stardust of yesterday

41:10.721 --> 41:17.561
The music of the years gone by

41:20.230 --> 41:24.651
Sometimes I wonder

41:25.652 --> 41:27.905
Why I spend

41:28.822 --> 41:32.618
The lonely night

41:33.285 --> 41:35.996
Dreaming of a song
